  "name": null,
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=2,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =7,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\nI. The stability function is $R(7Δx)=\\frac{1+7Δx/2}{1-7Δx/2}.$\n\nII. The stability region is $|\\frac{2-7Δx}{2+7Δx}|<1.$\n\nIII. The method is absolutely stable.\n\nIV. The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=0.5.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$",
